<Docs title="One visual language." intro="A shared set of shaders, with renderers built for the surfaces they inhabit.">
<h2>Web rendering</h2><p>The web package owns the GPU runtime, camera, shader pipeline, and glyph analysis. This site imports its React component; there is no second copy of the renderer hiding in the explorer.</p><div class="pipeline"><span>Scene + camera</span><b>→</b><span>Light + bloom</span><b>→</b><span>ASCII / raw</span></div><p>WebGL2 and WebGPU backends expose the same visual controls. Quality presets trade render resolution and sampling work against detail. ASCII is a rendering stage: it maps the scene's structure into glyphs, rather than placing a text texture over a photograph.</p>
<h2>Terminal rendering</h2><p>The Rust terminal path produces a character-based view through Ratatui. Ghostty has a different contract: a fragment shader receives the already-rendered terminal. Its integration adds a restrained animated background and can optionally distort the terminal texture.</p><p>The Ghostty effect is an artistic, single-pass adaptation. It does not reproduce the web renderer's ray integration, multipass bloom, or full physics.</p>
<h2>Origins and credits</h2><p>Blackhole was extracted from <a href="https://github.com/austindelic/portfolio">Austin Delic's portfolio</a>. The original renderer, amber palette, ASCII treatment, and reference artwork inform this project. Personal profile content is not included.</p><ul><li><a href="https://departuremono.com/">Departure Mono</a> by Helena Zhang supplies the interface typeface, distributed under the SIL Open Font License.</li><li><a href="https://astro.build/">Astro</a> and <a href="https://react.dev/">React</a> power the static site and interactive island.</li><li><a href="https://ratatui.rs/">Ratatui</a> and <a href="https://ghostty.org/">Ghostty</a> provide the terminal surfaces.</li></ul><p>Asset provenance and license notices live in <a href="/ASSET_NOTICES.txt">the asset notices</a>. Refer to the <a href="https://github.com/austindelic/blackhole">source repository</a> for code licensing and shader attribution.</p>
<h2>Working on Blackhole</h2><p>Keep renderer changes in the package, interface changes in the explorer, and terminal adaptations in their integration directories. Verify the actual rendered result on the target platform; a shader that compiles is only half the story.</p>
</Docs>
